WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.988
How does it run?

2
00:00:00.988 --> 00:00:02.963
Each stretch has something to prove.

3
00:00:02.963 --> 00:00:06.058
Pre-flight builds the
platform host as a Tier 0

4
00:00:06.058 --> 00:00:09.562
system and runs a read-only
assessment of the estate.

5
00:00:09.562 --> 00:00:12.348
It produces twenty-three deliverables,

6
00:00:12.348 --> 00:00:15.724
and G0 passes only with
no open critical finding.

7
00:00:15.724 --> 00:00:19.043
Foundation turns on the
Conditional Access baseline,

8
00:00:19.043 --> 00:00:22.287
but only after at least seven
days in report-only mode.

9
00:00:22.287 --> 00:00:27.087
The pilot is one division, measured
against eight numeric criteria, such as

10
00:00:27.087 --> 00:00:32.350
authentication success above 99 percent,
and held drift-free for an agreed period.

11
00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:34.300
Rollout then moves in waves.

12
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:39.537
Retirement takes things away, so nothing is
retired unless its rollback still works.

13
00:00:39.537 --> 00:00:43.888
And retired disks get sanitized,
because they hold password hashes.

14
00:00:43.888 --> 00:00:49.154
In steady state, reassessment runs weekly
and drift detection daily, and every

15
00:00:49.154 --> 00:00:54.338
severity has a clock: by default, a critical
finding is fixed within four hours.

16
00:00:54.338 --> 00:00:56.040
That leaves the decisions.
